{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016ctcS1ox97Si3G5NcZANyF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (utility implementations), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets), `docs/` (specifications).\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists on the working branch for `pkg/format/` (color.go, size.go, table.go) and `pkg/sys/` (stat.go, stat_darwin.go, stat_linux.go, terminal.go). No `pkg/testutils/` code exists yet. All releases show `codestatus: not started` in the current analysis.\n\n**Current release (00.0)**: Four use cases — uc001-magefiles (excluded by DD7), uc002-format (already implemented), uc003-sys (already implemented), uc004-testutils (not yet built). The only remaining buildable work in rel00.0 is `pkg/testutils/`.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nThe differential testing harness (`pkg/testutils/`) is the single remaining deliverable in release 00.0 that falls within generation scope. It is also a hard dependency for every subsequent utility implementation — no `cmd/` package can be verified without it. Per P2, implementation and tests must be separate tasks; this task covers implementation only.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/testutils DiffTest struct and differential runner (prd004-testutils R1, R2, R3, R4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd004-testutils.yaml (testutils PRD with requirement IDs -- if not found, glob for docs/specs/product-requirements/prd*testutils*.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml (concrete execution flow for differential testing harness)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (test suite for release 00.0 covering testutils acceptance)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/testutils component description, design decisions, data structures)\n      - pkg/sys/terminal.go (reference for project code style, copyright header, package doc comment)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (reference for project code style and doc comment conventions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"DiffTest struct, DiffResult struct, RunDiffTest runner function, normalization hook type\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define the DiffTest struct with fields for input arguments (string slice), stdin content (byte slice), environment variables (string slice), the path to the Go binary under test, and the path to the GNU reference binary. Field names and types must match the testutils PRD exactly.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement a RunDiffTest function that accepts a DiffTest, executes both the Go binary and the GNU reference binary with identical stdin, arguments, and environment via os/exec, captures stdout ([]byte), stderr ([]byte), and exit code (int) from each invocation, and returns a DiffResult.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"DiffResult must report whether the outputs match and, on divergence, include the input arguments that triggered the failure, expected output from the reference binary, actual output from the Go binary, and which streams diverged (stdout, stderr, exit code).\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Support normalization hooks -- caller-provided functions applied to both binary outputs before comparison -- so that known acceptable differences (e.g., timestamps, absolute paths) do not cause false test failures.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary source file is difftest.go because the primary exported type is DiffTest. Per project convention (ARCHITECTURE.yaml), package files are named after the primary exported type, not the package name -- testutils/testutils.go is forbidden.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the same copyright header (Copyright Petar Djukic, MIT), package doc comment style, and code conventions as pkg/sys/terminal.go and pkg/format/size.go.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"This package is a test helper library consumed by cmd/*_test.go files. It does not produce a standalone binary. It should be importable as github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/testutils/difftest.go exists and exports DiffTest, DiffResult, and RunDiffTest as public symbols.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"RunDiffTest executes both binaries via os/exec with identical stdin, args, and environment, and returns a DiffResult containing captured stdout, stderr, and exit code from each.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"When outputs diverge, DiffResult includes the input args, expected output (reference binary), actual output (Go binary), and identifies which stream(s) diverged.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/... compiles with no errors.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22067,"cache_read_input_tokens":19285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22067},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc621187-7a6a-4a5a-8f21-72a5b6856989","uuid":"1c251af5-5277-4fef-9fa0-181f162c2863"}
